  "narrative": {
    "intro": "New Tech Solutions has $324M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. New Tech Solutions received 1,985 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $163K. New Tech Solutions saw obligations down 45.6% year over year. New Tech Solutions' obligations rose from $478M in FY21 to $596M in FY25, then fell to $324M in FY26. New Tech Solutions' work in FY2026 to date concentrates in Other Computer Related Services at $295M, and the Department of Defense is the largest buying agency at $101M. This fiscal-year snapshot is partial, reflecting fiscal year to date totals rather than full-year results.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are New Tech Solutions' top federal customers?",
        "body": "Department of Defense obligated $101M. Department of Health and Human Services obligated $47.8M, and Department of Justice obligated $38.5M. Department of Homeland Security obligated $34.4M, Department of the Treasury obligated $18.1M, and Department of State obligated $17.6M. National Science Foundation obligated $12.6M, NASA obligated $10M, Department of Transportation obligated $7.3M, and Department of Energy obligated $4.1M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and products does New Tech Solutions sell to the government?",
        "body": "Other Computer Related Services is New Tech Solutions' largest market at $295M. Electronic Computer Manufacturing accounted for $21.2M and Software Publishers accounted for $4.8M. New Tech Solutions also recorded obligations in Computer Terminal and Other Computer Peripheral Equipment Manufacturing at $1.6M and several smaller manufacturing and business-support markets."
      }
    ]
  },
